WEBVTT

00:00:02.189 --> 00:00:07.440
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the thirty-first, bank holiday crew on Teams. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:13.859
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, unfortunately. The heating in the portakabin thinks it's midwinter. Absolutely roasting in here.</v>

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:18.539
<v Callum Reid>Luxury. Usually you can see your breath over the keyboard.</v>

00:00:19.129 --> 00:00:24.730
<v Jamie Brennan>I'm not reporting a fault, before anyone puts my name against it. Just having a moan.</v>

00:00:25.809 --> 00:00:28.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Noted, official moan received. Right, what's already closed out?</v>

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:34.600
<v Jamie Brennan>I signed off the inspection on the FLTs on Tuesday. That's all done, paperwork included.</v>

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Closed, then, not another job for this morning.</v>

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:47.090
<v Priya Raman>And I tested the line 2 guard yesterday and it's all fine now. Reset and interlock both behaved.</v>

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.219
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, no grief from it afterwards either.</v>

00:00:53.289 --> 00:01:02.740
<v Priya Raman>Also, we were going to replace the belt on the GT1 Compressor Section but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it. Not doing that today.</v>

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:09.090
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, off this meeting's list. Nothing to agree on that one.</v>

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:18.500
<v Fiona Doyle>Just an observation from the log: noticed the turbine two was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down.</v>

00:01:20.409 --> 00:01:24.260
<v David Whitfield>Settled back to normal, did it, rather than just stopped climbing?</v>

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:30.480
<v Fiona Doyle>Back to normal, yeah. Just context, I'm not raising any work off it.</v>

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:38.129
<v Callum Reid>The supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line one HPU either. Same blocker as before.</v>

00:01:40.609 --> 00:01:44.810
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, still no confirmed delivery. Nothing new to tell you from stores.</v>

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:51.140
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that stays blocked. We're not adding another chase for that here.</v>

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:59.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Davey, can you replace the seals on the booster pump today at 2pm? Top priority please.</v>

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:04.069
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, clipped the end there. Today at 2pm, seals done for then?</v>

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:11.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today at 2pm is the deadline. Top priority please, ahead of the lower-priority bits.</v>

00:02:13.289 --> 00:02:19.590
<v David Whitfield>Right, accepted. I'll replace the seals on the booster pump and have that done for today at 2pm.</v>

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:26.389
<v Fiona Doyle>So that's the top-priority one, not something squeezed in around the other work?</v>

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:29.960
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. That one comes first.</v>

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:38.080
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet next week? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:02:38.439 --> 00:02:44.389
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, just separating that from the inspection we've already mentioned. These are the pre-use checks next week?</v>

00:02:45.699 --> 00:02:50.250
<v Jamie Brennan>That's it. The FLTs inspection I mentioned is signed off already. Different bit.</v>

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:58.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet next week. Fairly important, but not pulling it into today.</v>

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.219
<v Priya Raman>Understood. I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet next week.</v>

00:03:06.229 --> 00:03:11.479
<v Callum Reid>Yep, next week. Heard you both, even with that lovely robot noise in the middle.</v>

00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:16.900
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you send the shift handover report round by 11am as well?</v>

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:24.810
<v Priya Raman>Um, no, sorry. I can't take the handover report on. That needs to go to someone else.</v>

00:03:27.169 --> 00:03:34.169
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, not with PR then. Cal, can you take it instead and send the shift handover report round by 11am?</v>

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:39.430
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll take that. I'll send the shift handover report round by 11am.</v>

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.400
<v Fiona Doyle>That's moved over, then, rather than both of you having it?</v>

00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:48.689
<v Callum Reid>Just me, yeah. No duplicate report from PR.</v>

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:56.189
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Compressed Air Dryer by Thursday. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:59.870
<v David Whitfield>Low priority still? Not competing with the seals?</v>

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:06.610
<v Sarah Okafor>No, definitely low priority. I'll have the sensors recalibrated by Thursday, no change to that.</v>

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.860
<v Fiona Doyle>Okay, Sarah against the Compressed Air Dryer sensors, by Thursday.</v>

00:04:13.289 --> 00:04:14.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:26.759
<v David Whitfield>Yeah so, I'll chase the purchase order for the Gas Turbine 2 tomorrow at 9:30. It's in the 'if you've got a spare minute' category, not an urgent one.</v>

00:04:29.259 --> 00:04:35.209
<v Jamie Brennan>Dave, just the purchase order for the Gas Turbine 2, yeah? Separate from that blocked HPU delivery.</v>

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:42.100
<v David Whitfield>Exactly. Just chasing that purchase order, tomorrow at 9:30. Not taking on the HPU delivery chase.</v>

00:04:44.269 --> 00:04:50.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, keeping that as an if you've got a spare minute job, not promoting it up the list.</v>

00:04:52.089 --> 00:04:55.939
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, that's what I meant. I'll take it on that basis.</v>

00:04:58.019 --> 00:05:06.420
<v Fiona Doyle>There's also a site visit at the substation with the contractor needing doing, if you've got a spare minute. Hasn't got anyone against it.</v>

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:14.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to take that site visit at the substation with the contractor? Only if you've got a spare minute.</v>

00:05:16.509 --> 00:05:19.310
<v Priya Raman>Not me, sorry. Can't offer to take that.</v>

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.660
<v David Whitfield>Nor me. Not putting my hand up for that one.</v>

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:30.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay... no takers. That stays unowned, then. We're not treating the visit as agreed with anyone.</v>

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:35.829
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, still needs doing, but nobody against it and no date agreed.</v>

00:05:36.709 --> 00:05:45.110
<v Callum Reid>On a much less technical note, the charity bake sale on Friday was decent. Whoever made that lemon cake knew what they were doing.</v>

00:05:47.589 --> 00:05:51.790
<v Jamie Brennan>You had enough of it to carry out a statistically valid test.</v>

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:56.709
<v Callum Reid>Quality assurance, mate. All finished now, sadly. Especially the lemon cake.</v>

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:03.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes the cake review meeting—quick check we've all got the same picture.</v>

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:12.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Davey has the booster pump seals, top priority, today at 2pm. That's the one with the immediate deadline.</v>

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.850
<v David Whitfield>Yes, agreed. No confusion there.</v>

00:06:17.129 --> 00:06:22.730
<v Priya Raman>And I've got the Forklift Fleet pre-use checks next week, fairly important. Not the handover report.</v>

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.839
<v Callum Reid>Report's mine, round by 11am. Yep.</v>

00:06:27.759 --> 00:06:31.959
<v Sarah Okafor>And my Compressed Air Dryer sensor recalibration is low priority, by Thursday.</v>

00:06:33.269 --> 00:06:38.519
<v Jamie Brennan>All clear here. My inspection update was completed work, nothing new taken on by stores.</v>

00:06:39.689 --> 00:06:46.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. The substation visit still has nobody taking it, and the blocked and cancelled bits stay as discussed. Cheers, everyone.</v>
